cff-version: 1.2.0
version: 0.5.0
title: "Perception-XAlpha Lite: falsification-first formulaic factor research"
message: "If you use this framework or its measurements, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: xuxingjiankr-cpu
    website: "https://github.com/xuxingjiankr-cpu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xuxingjiankr-cpu/perception-xalpha-lite"
url: "https://xuxingjiankr-cpu.github.io/perception-xalpha-lite/"
abstract: >-
  A research framework that synthesises bounded symbolic factors, backtests them on
  point-in-time data with explicit costs and tradability constraints, and subjects every
  candidate to counterfactual controls, purged walk-forward validation, probability of
  backtest overfitting, and deflated Sharpe correction before it may be believed. It
  deliberately contains no execution path and makes no profitability claim. Includes measured
  estimates of four common backtest biases, and a reproducible demonstration that hindsight
  factor selection manufactures an information ratio of 4.53 from data with zero true edge.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - backtest overfitting
  - factor investing
  - deflated Sharpe ratio
  - point-in-time data
  - reproducible research
  - multiple testing
license: MIT
